    "raw_text": "Traffic Update - July 10, 2026 - Senator Farry\nView this email in a browser\nPennDOT Completes Major Construction on Langhorne-Yardley Intersection Improvement in Middletown Township\nPennDOT announced today that major construction has been completed on a project to improve travel and safety on Langhorne-Yardley Road through the Bridgetown Pike and Woodbourne Road intersections in Middletown Township.\nWhile major construction has been completed, drivers may encounter periodic single lane closures over the next several weeks to allow PennDOT’s contractor to perform final construction activities.\nUnder this contract, PennDOT’s contractor constructed:\nnew single-lane roundabout at Langhorne-Yardley Road and Bridgetown Pike\nrealigned roadway and added turning lanes\nupgraded traffic signals, ADA curb ramps, signage, and lighting\nImproved mobility for pedestrians and bicyclists.\nFor more information on the project, including pedestrian and bicyclist improvements, visit the\nLanghorne-Yardley Road Intersection Improvement Project webpage\n.\nHarrisburg Office\n351 Main Capitol\nHarrisburg, PA 17120\nPhone: 717-787-5072\nLanghorne Office\n370 East Maple Avenue, Suite 203\nLanghorne, PA 19047\nM-F: 9AM to 4:30 PM\nPhone: 215-638-1784\nWant to change how you receive these emails?\nYou can\nupdate your preferences\nor\nunsubscribe\n2026 © Senate of Pennsylvania |\nhttps://senatorfarry.com\n|\nPrivacy Policy",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "PennDOT has completed major construction work on an intersection improvement project on Langhorne-Yardley Road in Middletown Township, Bucks County. The project added a roundabout, realigned roads, added turning lanes, and upgraded traffic signals, pedestrian ramps, and lighting. Some single-lane closures may continue for several more weeks for finishing work.",
