    "raw_text": "Traffic Update - July 18, 2026 - Senator Farry\nView this email in a browser\nUpper Southampton Municipal Authority Utility Improvements to Close Maple Avenue\nPennDOT announced that Upper Southampton Municipal Authority will be performing utility improvements on Maple Avenue in Bucks County, beginning on Monday, July 27.\nDrivers are advised of the following travel restriction:\nMonday, July 27, through Monday, October 19, from 9:00 AM to 3:00 PM,\nMaple Avenue will be closed and detoured weekdays between Route 132 (Street Road) and Route 232 (Second Street Pike)\n. During the closure, drivers will be directed to use Route 132 (Street Road) and Route 232 (Second Street Pike).\nLocal access will be maintained at all times. Drivers are advised to allow extra time when traveling near the work area or along the detour route because backups and delays may occur. All scheduled activities are weather dependent.\nIf you are not already subscribed to this newsletter please sign up here\n.\nHarrisburg Office\n351 Main Capitol\nHarrisburg, PA 17120\nPhone: 717-787-5072\nLanghorne Office\n370 East Maple Avenue, Suite 203\nLanghorne, PA 19047\nM-F: 9AM to 4:30 PM\nPhone: 215-638-1784\nWant to change how you receive these emails?\nYou can\nupdate your preferences\nor\nunsubscribe\n2026 © Senate of Pennsylvania |\nhttps://senatorfarry.com\n|\nPrivacy Policy",
