    "raw_text": "Traffic Update - August 1, 2026 - Senator Farry\nTraffic Update - August 1, 2026 - Senator Farry\nView this email in a browser\nAqua Pennsylvania Utility Installation to Close Brownsville Road Weekdays in Bensalem Township\nPennDOT announced that Aqua Pennsylvania will perform utility installation on Brownsville Road in Bensalem Township, beginning on Monday, August 17.\nDrivers are advised of the following travel restriction:\nMonday, August 17, through Friday, October 30, from 9:00 AM to 3:00 PM,\nBrownsville Road will be closed and detoured weekdays between Carver Avenue and Dara Faith Drive\n. During the closure, drivers will be directed to use Old Street Road, Route 132 (Street Road), Route 532 (Bustleton Pike), Route 213 (Bridgetown Pike), and Bristol Road.\nLocal access will be maintained. Drivers are advised to allow extra time when traveling near the work area or through the detour route because backups and delays may occur. All scheduled activities are weather dependent.\nPennDOT Announced Resurfacing on Bensalem Road\nMotorists are advised of the following travel restriction:\nWednesday, August 5, through Friday, August 7, from 9:00 AM to 3:00 PM and from 7:00 PM to 5:00 AM the following morning, a lane closure with flagging will be in place on Route 513 (Hulmeville Road) between Route 132 (Street Road) and Galloway Road in Bensalem Township for paving and utility adjustments.\nIf you are not already subscribed to this newsletter please sign up here\n.\nHarrisburg Office\n351 Main Capitol\nHarrisburg, PA 17120\nPhone: 717-787-5072\nLanghorne Office\n370 East Maple Avenue, Suite 203\nLanghorne, PA 19047\nM-F: 9AM to 4:30 PM\nPhone: 215-638-1784\nWant to change how you receive these emails?\nYou can\nupdate your preferences\nor\nunsubscribe\n2026 © Senate of Pennsylvania |\nhttps://senatorfarry.com\n|\nPrivacy Policy",
    "ai_summary": {
