    "title": "Traffic Update – August 15, 2026",
    "url": "https://senatorfarry.com/enews/traffic-081526/",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Traffic Update - August 15, 2026 - Senator Farry\nTraffic Update - August 15, 2026 - Senator Farry\nView this email in a browser\nResurfacing Operations Planned Next Week on State Highway in Bensalem\nPennDOT announced that resurfacing operations are planned next week on Hulmeville Rd. in Bensalem. Drivers are advised of the following travel restrictions:\nMonday, August 17, through Friday, August 21, from 7:00 PM to 5:00 AM the following morning, a lane closure with flagging will be in place on\nRoute 513 (Hulmeville Road) between Route 132 (Street Road) and Galloway Road\nin Bensalem Township for paving.\nDrivers are advised to allow extra time when traveling through the work areas because backups and delays will occur. All scheduled activities are weather dependent.\nUnder these resurfacing and improvement projects, PennDOT’s contractors are repairing, milling, and repaving state highways with new asphalt pavement that will seal roadways and provide motorists with a safer and smoother riding surface.\nAqua Pennsylvania Utility Installation to Close Brownsville Road Weekdays in Bensalem\nPennDOT announced that Aqua Pennsylvania will perform utility installation on Brownsville Road in Bensalem Township, beginning on Monday, August 17.\nDrivers are advised of the following travel restriction:\nMonday, August 17, through Friday, October 30, from 9:00 AM to 3:00 PM,\nBrownsville Road will be closed and detoured weekdays between Carver Avenue and Dara Faith Drive\n. During the closure, drivers will be directed to use Old Street Road, Route 132 (Street Road), Route 532 (Bustleton Pike), Route 213 (Bridgetown Pike), and Bristol Road.\nLocal access will be maintained. Drivers are advised to allow extra time when traveling near the work area or through the detour route because backups and delays may occur. All scheduled activities are weather dependent.\nIf you are not already subscribed to this newsletter please sign up here\n.\nHarrisburg Office\n351 Main Capitol\nHarrisburg, PA 17120\nPhone: 717-787-5072\nLanghorne Office\n370 East Maple Avenue, Suite 203\nLanghorne, PA 19047\nM-F: 9AM to 4:30 PM\nPhone: 215-638-1784\nWant to change how you receive these emails?\nYou can\nupdate your preferences\nor\nunsubscribe\n2026 © Senate of Pennsylvania |\nhttps://senatorfarry.com\n|\nPrivacy Policy",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Senator Farry's office distributed a traffic advisory relaying two PennDOT announcements affecting Bensalem Township. The first is a nightly lane closure on Hulmeville Road (Route 513) for paving work August 17-21, and the second is a full weekday closure of Brownsville Road from August 17 through October 30 for an Aqua Pennsylvania utility installation, with a designated detour route.",
